    <string name="help_faq_link_q">How do I link a phone to the business?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_link_a">On the new phone open the app and choose “Link this phone with a code”: you will see a short code. Then, on the owner’s or an admin’s phone, go to More → Team → Phones and type that code. The phone is linked and cashiers sign in with their PIN.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_offline_q">What happens if the internet goes down?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_offline_a">Nothing stops: the app keeps selling, recording credit sales and expenses, and saves everything on the phone. When the connection returns, whatever is pending is sent by itself, exactly once. Reports on the web panel catch up when the phones finish syncing.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_closing_q">How does the daily close work?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_closing_a">The close is automatic: nobody opens or closes anything. Each business day runs from one day’s cutoff time (2:00 AM by default) to the next, so what is sold at 1 AM counts for the previous day, and “yesterday” is yesterday 2:00 AM to today 2:00 AM. In More → Daily close you see, per day, sales by payment method, expenses, withdrawals and the expected cash = cash sales + cash credit payments + cash in − drawer expenses − withdrawals. Transfers, card and credit do not go in the drawer.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_import_q">How do I import my products from a file?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_import_a">Importing is done in the web panel: in Inventory choose “Import CSV”. The file has one row per product with columns such as name, code, price, cost, unit, category and stock. First you see a preview of what would be created or updated, without saving anything; then you confirm. If you import again, what already exists is updated and not duplicated.</string>
